Requirements
------------

XBoing has been migrated from X11/XPM to raylib and Premake 5. No external X
server or XPM installation is required to build or run the game; raylib is
vendored as a git submodule under `raylib/`.

- A C11-compatible compiler:
    + Windows: Visual Studio 2022 / MSBuild or W64DevKit (GCC + GNU Make)
    + Linux: GCC or Clang + GNU Make (`build-essential`), plus standard OpenGL,
      ALSA, and windowing development headers required by raylib
    + macOS: Xcode Command Line Tools (`xcode-select --install`)
- Premake 5 (`premake5` / `premake5.exe` placed in the repository root)
- Initialized `raylib` git submodule:

    git submodule update --init --recursive


Project Generation & Compilation
--------------------------------

Generate build files from `premake5.lua` at the repository root, then compile
the `rayboing` target.

Linux / macOS (GNU Make):

    ./premake5 gmake
    make rayboing                # Debug build (default)
    make rayboing config=release # Release build

Windows (Visual Studio / MSBuild):

    .\premake5.exe vs2022
    msbuild xboing.sln -p:Configuration=Debug -m

Detailed platform-specific setup guides are located in:

    docs/setup/getting-started.md
    docs/building/gmake.md
    docs/building/msbuild.md
    docs/building/visual-studio.md
    docs/building/w64devkit.md


Running XBoing
--------------

Compiled binaries are written to `bin/Debug/` and `bin/Release/`. Run the
executable from the repository root so relative asset paths under `resource/`
resolve properly:

    ./bin/Debug/rayboing
    ./bin/Debug/rayboing resource/levels/level01.data


HighScore File
--------------

High scores are automatically read from and saved to `scores.txt` in the
working directory when a game ends.
